# TV Show App: Low-Token Core Context

Use this as the default decision context. Keep responses and implementations aligned with these constraints only.

## Product Scope
- Build 3 views: Home (genre rows), Show Details, Search by show name.
- Use TVMaze API data; derive genre groups from show index; sort each genre by rating desc.
- Include loading, error, and empty states (skeletons on main loading paths).
- Support responsive UI + light/dark theme with persisted preference.

## Architecture Boundaries
- Stack: Vue 3 + Composition API + TypeScript, Vue Router, Tailwind, Pinia, Vue Query, vue-i18n.
- Views orchestrate; reusable rendering stays in components.
- Business logic lives in composables/pure utilities, not large components.
- Keep API mapping/adapters separate from UI.

## State Rules (strict)
- Vue Query: server data lifecycle (fetch/cache/stale/retry/loading/error).
- Pinia: UI/cross-view preferences only.
- Do not duplicate server data in Pinia.

## Quality Rules
- TypeScript strict mindset; avoid `any` unless isolated and justified.
- No hardcoded user-facing strings in components; use `t(...)` keys.
- Prioritize accessibility (semantic structure, keyboard/focus visibility).
- Maintain clean runtime (no console errors, no dead code, no hidden side effects).

## Delivery Checklist
- Keep changes small, testable, and production-oriented.
- Add/update Vitest tests for critical business logic and UI states.
- Ensure lint/type/build pass before considering task complete.
